package com.noop.ui

// MARK: - Body-age contour keyframes (SQ10, from the Ridge board's `Baseline` body-age hero)
//
// The board draws eight nested contours, each morphing through three keyframe shapes (a fourth returns to the
// first, so the loop is seamless). Re-deriving them as trig would drift from the board; this is the board's own
// geometry, resampled from 140 to [RING_POINTS] points per shape — the closed Catmull-Rom spline in [BodyAgeHero]
// rebuilds the smoothness — in the board's 300 x 300 unit space, as tenths of a unit so they stay integers.
//
// Layout: ring-major, then keyframe: entry `ring * 3 + key`, each `x y x y …` for [RING_POINTS] points. Parsed
// once, lazily, into [BODY_AGE_RING_KEYS]; nothing reads the strings after that.

/** Points kept per keyframe shape. */
internal const val RING_POINTS = 35

/** Keyframe shapes per ring (the board's fourth keyframe repeats the first, so it is not stored). */
internal const val RING_KEYS = 3

/** The board's rings, outermost last. */
internal const val RING_COUNT = 8

